    <DataNode elementId="CPD-12727" textLabel="wogonin" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="XLTFNNCXVBYBSX-UHFFFAOYSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="520.2321166992188" centerY="1550.0" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, zhang, SRI, caspi">Wogonin is an O-methylated 4&apos;-deoxyflavone found in |FRAME: TAX-65409|. It induces apoptosis in a wide spectrum of human tumor cells &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; and inhibits tumor growth &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; in different mouse tumor models |CITS: [27152350]|. The glycosides of wogonin are known as wogonosides. |FRAME: CPD-12728 Oroxindin| is a wogonin glucuronide isolated from |FRAME: TAX-83951|.</Comment>
